# The one declaration. Every database table, Ecto row, wire table, Rust
# constant and TypeScript type is read from this file; nothing else names a
# table, column, enum, command, frame or refusal.
#
# Lines (a `#` starts a comment; indentation is cosmetic):
#
#   domain <name>...                 each before `system` carries the next mask
#                                    bit (1 2 4 8); `system` carries none and is
#                                    in no mask. A bit is stored in api_keys
#                                    masks: a migration dropping a domain
#                                    rewrites them.
#   frame <NAME> <id>                wire frame kinds
#   layout <n>                       the byte layout native/wire implements; in
#                                    wire_hash, so a client of another refuses
#   dict <text|frame> <id> <fnv>     a zstd dictionary, in wire_hash
#   enum <name> <value>...           codes are 0-based declaration order
#   carry <enum>...                  enums the frames carry (NACK, BYE, op verbs);
#                                    an enum enters wire_hash when a resident,
#                                    wire or projection column, a command param
#                                    or this line names it
#   table <name> <domain> <residency> [append_only] [soft_delete] [global] [account_optional] [singleton]
#       residency: resident (the kernel derives from it; on the wire)
#                  server   (never leaves the server)
#                  wire     (derived on the wire, never stored)
#       global: no account_id (accounts, magic_links)
#       account_optional: account_id may be null (audit before sign-in)
#       singleton: one row per account
#       unmasked: in no key's mask, whatever its domain (citations)
#       soft_delete: a drop leaves a tombstone (deleted_at set); its keys and
#                  uniques hold over live rows only, and reads pass over it
#   projection <name> <domain> <source table> where <sql>
#     pick <col>...                  a resident view of a server table, not stored
#   natural <col>... [where <w>]     the key a KEYED put names; per account. A where
#                                    (keys, indexes, projections) is one of
#                                    col = 'value', col is null, col is not null
#   unique <col>... [global] [where <w>]   per account unless `global`
#   index <col> [desc]... [global] [where <w>]   per account (account_id leads,
#                                    so a key never names it) unless `global`
#   cap <n>                          most rows per account (`cap` refusal); every
#                                    stored table an account owns has one
#   col <name> <type> [<target>] [! | ?] [= <default>] [flag]...
#   metric <name> <u32|i64|f64> [flag]...   nullable; implies `<name>_on day ?`;
#                                    a write needs `as_of` and makes a citation
#   prose <name> [flag]...           text ?; a write needs `source` and
#                                    `expect_rev` and makes a citation
#   retired table <n>                ids are append-only: <n> tables or projections
#                                    once declared here keep their numbers
#   retired col <n>                  inside a table: <n> columns once declared here
#                                    keep their ids (dropped by a hand-written step)
#   group <words>                    the columns after it fall under it (World's
#                                    column groups); presentation only, in no hash
#   command <name> [<col> | <name>:<type>[?]]... [human_only]
#                                    params are table columns or typed free params
#
# Types: id ref(<table>) enum(<enum>) bool u8 u32 i64 f64 day time str text json bytes
# Flags: ! required (NOT NULL)   ? nullable (the default)
#        private (browser sessions only, never a key)   server_only (never leaves the server)   human_only (a key's write is
#        refused `human_only`)   readonly (the server or a command writes it, never a
#        put)   unique (per account)   cascade (a nullable ref whose row is deleted
#        with the row it names; without it a nullable ref is set null)   loose (a ref
#        that is a plain id: no foreign key, no tenant trigger, so a purge of the row
#        it names never rewrites it; for append-only rows and the ledger)
# Names are lowercase words ([a-z][a-z0-9_]*), frames uppercase; tokens are
# separated by spaces and tabs. A default is a value of its column's type
# (true/false, an integer in range, a decimal, a 'quoted' text, an enum value).
# A metric's _on twin is readonly and as visible as its metric.
#
# Null (the codec's rule, native/wire): in BOOT/PATCH a u32 run carries null as
# 0xFFFFFFFF (so an id, ref, day, time or enum code never takes it; bool is 0, 1
# or null), str as the empty string, i64 as i64::MIN, f64 as NaN. NULL and '' are one value: a put of '' or of zero-length
# text is stored as NULL, so no column holds ''. In OPS a cell of type 0 with
# length 0 clears its column; a u32 0xFFFFFFFF, an i64::MIN or a NaN cell is
# refused `type`. Wire type codes: 1 u32 (id ref bool u8 u32 day time enum;
# day = days since 0000-01-01, proleptic Gregorian (Elixir's
# Date.to_gregorian_days/1), 0 to 3652424 = 9999-12-31, past which a cell is
# refused `type`; time = unix seconds), 2 str (str text json, json any JSON value),
# 3 i64, 4 f64; the codec may
# also run a column as 6 sym (a dictionary of strs) or 7 list (u32 ids).
# A PATCH deletes rows with a block of their own table whose only column is
# 0xFFFE (u32 ids). A BYE's reason is its `bye` enum code; an op's verb byte
# is its `verb` code + 1 (put 1, drop 2, command 3).
#
# Implied on every stored table, in this order and with these column ids:
#   1 id   2 account_id (not on `global`)   3 rev   4 inserted_at   5 updated_at
#   6 deleted_at (only on `soft_delete`)
# Declared columns take ids from 8 in declaration order; a metric's `_on` twin
# takes the id after it. Tables and projections are numbered from 1, commands
# from 1, in declaration order. A required `ref` cascades on delete; a nullable
# one is set null.

domain world desk mail corpus system

layout 4
# priv/wire/<name>.zdict: a text cell of 256 bytes or more packs against
# `text`, a ZSTD body against `frame`.
dict text 1213355092 7083223
dict frame 1213351506 3169144972

frame HELLO 1
frame WELCOME 2
frame BOOT 3
frame PATCH 4
frame OPS 8
frame ACK 9
frame NACK 10
frame TICK 11
frame PING 13
frame PONG 14
frame BYE 16
frame RPC 33
frame REPLY 34

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- enums

enum refusal scope human_only lease_missing leased column type not_found natural_key stage fire_hold heat lineage_busy cooldown freshness stale rev source_missing source_trust too_large rate cap internal burst rule blob_missing unlinked fire step_up

carry refusal bye verb

enum verb put drop command
enum actor operator agent system mail
enum bye revoked grants restart schema suspended

enum account_status active suspended
enum provider email github x
enum factor_kind totp webauthn
enum challenge_kind totp_enroll webauthn_register webauthn_assert email_step_up

enum stage discovered freshness gated in_batch draft_ready fire_ready open_fire submitted reply closed
enum app_status open paused hired closed
enum freshness open thin closed blocked
enum gate pursue maybe skip
enum band frontier labs big_tech systems craft mid thin kill
enum outcome offer rejected ghosted withdrawn declined expired skipped
enum work_mode onsite hybrid remote
enum employment full_time part_time contract internship freelance
enum app_channel listing referral recruiter cold other inbound
enum listing_format text markdown html

enum batch_kind day_pack leftover universe_gaps linkedin
enum batch_status draft_prep fire_ready open_fire closed
enum fire hold open_fire

enum item_kind experience project education skill timeline fact
enum overlay_mode tailor add drop
enum cv_accent ink signal paper
enum cv_density cv tight narrative

enum place_kind country city state province
enum ownership private public subsidiary nonprofit government
enum remote_policy onsite hybrid remote remote_first
enum office_kind hq engineering sales regional other
enum source_kind official filing statistics news ratings review blog other

enum relation recruiter hiring_manager engineer referral founder other
# The OutreachItem's variant: what a mission produces and what an outreach
# row is. A channel that earns rows of its own is appended here.
enum outreach_kind email careers_page linkedin x_dm discord other note
enum direction outbound inbound
enum filing filed unfiled ignored
enum filer matcher operator agent mail
enum mail_pipe gmail domain hireme

enum cv_format markdown pdf docx composed doc
enum language_level a1 a2 b1 b2 c1 c2 native

# Retired: a mission's kind is outreach_kind (the outreach it produces is
# its kind); kept declared while the MCP's tool schema and the page's route
# select still name it.
enum mission_kind email careers_page linkedin x_dm discord other
enum mission_state draft draft_ready fire_ready in_flight fired cancelled
enum confirmation provisional confirmed
enum request_status open granted declined
enum prior_send applied not_applied
enum mail_provider gmail
enum mailbox_status linking live auth_failed error unlinked

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- system

table accounts system server global
  col name str ?
  col status enum account_status ! = active
  # Committed account writes, bumped by the sequencer with each one.
  col desk_rev i64 ! = 0
  # The next applications.no; a number is never reused.
  col next_no u32 ! = 1
  # Announcing audit events, bumped by Audit.record in the same write: the
  # account lens's cursor, one row read instead of a scan of the trail.
  # Text bytes the account stores (str, text and json cells), kept
  # by the sequencer in the write that changes them; past
  # Security.account_text_bytes a write is refused `cap`.
  col text_bytes i64 ! = 0 readonly

table sessions system server
  cap 10000
  index revoked_at
  col token_hash bytes ! server_only
  unique token_hash global
  col authenticated_at time !
  col mfa_at time ?
  col last_seen_at time !
  col expires_at time !
  col revoked_at time ?
  col ip str ?
  col user_agent str ?
  # Signed in with "Remember this device": the remembered lifetimes (Security).
  col remember bool ?

table identities system server
  cap 100
  unique provider subject global
  col provider enum provider !
  col subject str !
  col display str ?
  col verified_at time !

table magic_links system server global
  index email expires_at
  col email str !
  col token_hash bytes ! server_only
  unique token_hash global
  col expires_at time !
  col used_at time ?
  col ip str ?
  col user_agent str ?

table api_keys system server
  cap 1000
  unique key_id global
  col key_id str !
  col name str !
  col secret_hash bytes ! server_only
  col prefix str !
  col read_mask u8 ! = 0
  col write_mask u8 ! = 0
  col may_delete bool ! = false
  col last_used_at time ?
  col expires_at time ?
  col revoked_at time ?
  # Set when the operator revokes a key's lease; Keys.resume clears it.
  col paused_at time ? readonly

table factors system server
  cap 100
  index kind
  unique credential_id global where credential_id is not null
  col kind enum factor_kind !
  col name str ?
  col totp_secret bytes ? server_only
  col totp_last_step i64 ?
  col credential_id bytes ?
  col public_key bytes ?
  col sign_count u32 ?
  col aaguid bytes ?
  col transports str ?
  col backup_eligible bool ?
  col backed_up bool ?
  col verified_at time ?
  col last_used_at time ?
  col consecutive_failures u32 ! = 0
  col disabled_at time ?

table challenges system server
  cap 10000
  index session_id
  col session_id ref sessions !
  col kind enum challenge_kind !
  col payload bytes ! server_only
  col expires_at time !

table recovery_codes system server
  cap 100
  col salt bytes ! server_only
  col code_hash bytes ! server_only
  col used_at time ?

table audit system server append_only account_optional
  cap 10000000
  index id desc
  # The trail purge reads expiring kinds past a date across every account.
  index kind inserted_at global
  # The account trail's security view pages by it: (account_id, security, id desc).
  index security id desc
  col kind str !
  col ip str ?
  col user_agent str ?
  col meta json ?
  col key_id ref api_keys ? loose
  col session_id ref sessions ? loose
  # Set at insert from the kind: a security event (kept forever), not
  # activity (expires). A row whose writer leaves it out reads as security.
  col security bool ! = true readonly

table outbox system server
  cap 100000
  # The drain reads due notices across every account.
  index next_at global where sent_at is null
  col address str !
  col kind str !
  col meta json ?
  col attempts u32 ! = 0
  col next_at time !
  col sent_at time ?
  col last_error str ?

# A resent op_id that was ACKed answers its ACK and writes nothing; a refused
# op is not kept, so its writer may send it again once fixed. Rows age out
# after 24 h, and at the cap an account's oldest make room.
table op_ledger system server
  cap 1000000
  # An op_id is the writer's own: two keys, or a key and the operator, may
  # pick the same one.
  unique writer op_id
  index inserted_at
  col op_id i64 !
  col key_id ref api_keys ? loose
  col verb enum verb !
  # A table id for put and drop, a command id for command.
  col subject u32 !
  col target u32 ?
  col row_id u32 ?
  col ack_rev i64 ?
  # The key that wrote the op, 0 for the operator (key_id is null then).
  col writer u32 ! = 0

# Hosts whose pages may source `culture` and ratings. Operator-owned.
table trusted_hosts system server
  cap 1000
  unique host
  col host str !
  col note text ?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- corpus

table profiles corpus resident
  cap 100
  unique slug
  col slug str !
  col name str !
  col headline str ?
  col summary text ?
  col narrative text ?
  col narrative_private text ? private

# CV atoms; a null profile_id is shared by every profile.
table items corpus resident
  cap 10000
  unique key
  index profile_id kind
  # A profile's own items go with it; a shared item has no profile.
  col profile_id ref profiles ? cascade
  col kind enum item_kind !
  col key str !
  col title str !
  col body text ?
  col org str ?
  col span str ?
  col position u32 ! = 0
  # U+001F-joined.
  col keywords str ?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- desk

table applications desk resident
  natural canonical_url where canonical_url is not null
  cap 50000
  index stage
  index corporation_id
  index batch_id
  col no u32 ! unique readonly
  col corporation_id ref corporations ?
  col place_id ref places ?
  col contact_id ref contacts ?
  col batch_id ref batches ?
  col company str ?
  col role str ?
  col location str ?
  col work_mode enum work_mode ?
  col employment enum employment ?
  col comp_raw str ?
  col channel enum app_channel ?
  col listing_raw text ?
  col listing_format enum listing_format ?
  col listing_url str ?
  col canonical_url str ?
  col listing_on day ?
  # The kernel's extraction from listing_raw at write time, U+001F-joined.
  col keywords str ? readonly
  col keywords_version u32 ? readonly
  col source_id ref sources ?
  col stage enum stage ! = discovered readonly
  # One char per stage, D A P S B.
  col pips str ? readonly
  col stage_on day ? readonly
  col stage_notes json ?
  col status enum app_status ! = open
  col gate enum gate ?
  col freshness enum freshness ?
  col heat_override bool ! = false readonly
  col heat_override_reason str ? readonly
  col score_100 u8 ?
  # Set by the stage command as it moves (submitted, reply, closed); heat
  # decays an application's load from the later of applied_on and replied_on.
  col applied_on day ? readonly
  col replied_on day ? readonly
  col closed_on day ? readonly
  col outcome enum outcome ?
  col notes text ?
  col battleplan text ?
  col letter_raw text ?
  col cv_theme json ?
  command stage stage note:text? outcome?
  command note stage body:text
  command heat_override reason:str
  command open_fire human_only
  # The CV it goes out with: a pin by the operator or an agent (pick_cv) over
  # the rules' pick, and the version frozen as it is submitted.
  col cv_root_id ref cv_roots ? readonly
  col cv_pinned_by enum actor ? readonly
  col cv_version_id ref cv_versions ? readonly
  # A send the crucible ledger recorded (stage_notes sync.applied_on) that no
  # one has settled: its missions cannot fire until the operator says whether
  # it went out.
  col prior_send enum prior_send ? human_only
  command pick_cv cv_root_id
  command unpin_cv

table events desk resident append_only
  cap 1000000
  index application_id id desc
  col application_id ref applications !
  col kind str !
  col body text ?
  col actor enum actor ! readonly
  col key_id ref api_keys ? readonly loose
  col op_id i64 ? readonly

table batches desk resident
  cap 10000
  unique code
  col code str !
  col ordinal u32 !
  col kind enum batch_kind ! = day_pack
  col status enum batch_status ! = draft_prep
  col fire enum fire ! = hold human_only
  col target_size u32 ! = 55
  col queued_on day ?
  col note text ?

table cv_lineages desk resident
  cap 50000
  unique corporation_id
  col corporation_id ref corporations !
  col generation u32 ! = 1 readonly
  col opened_on day ! readonly
  col rewrites_allowed bool ! = true
  col theme json ?
  command open_generation corporation_id

table cv_overlays desk resident
  cap 500000
  unique application_id item_id
  col application_id ref applications !
  col item_id ref items !
  col lineage_id ref cv_lineages ?
  col mode enum overlay_mode !
  col title str ?
  col body text ?
  col reason text ?
  col generation u32 ! = 1 readonly

table settings desk resident singleton
  cap 1
  # gym_target and net_lane_url, the lanes' own.
  retired col 2
  col goal_total u32 ?
  col goal_on day ?
  col goal_daily u32 ?
  col heat_config json ?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- world

table places world resident
  natural iso2 where kind = 'country'
  natural geonames_id where kind = 'city'
  natural geonames_id where kind = 'state'
  natural geonames_id where kind = 'province'
  cap 100000
  index country_id name
  # The world lens and agents look places up by name and filter by region.
  index name
  index region population
  group identity
  col kind enum place_kind !
  col country_id ref places ?
  col iso2 str ?
  col iso3 str ?
  col geonames_id u32 ?
  col name str !
  col region str ?
  col subregion str ?
  col lat f64 ?
  col lon f64 ?
  col timezone str ?
  col currency str ?
  group demography
  metric population u32
  metric area_km2 f64
  metric density_per_km2 f64
  metric median_age f64
  metric urban_share f64
  metric foreign_born_share f64
  metric english_proficiency f64
  group economy
  metric gdp_usd f64
  metric gdp_per_capita_usd f64
  metric gdp_ppp_usd f64
  metric gdp_per_capita_ppp_usd f64
  metric gdp_growth f64
  metric inflation f64
  metric unemployment f64
  metric median_income_usd f64
  metric cost_of_living_index f64
  metric rent_index f64
  metric income_tax_top f64
  group liveability
  metric qol_index f64
  metric hdi f64
  metric safety_index f64
  metric healthcare_index f64
  metric pollution_index f64
  metric climate_index f64
  metric internet_mbps f64
  group energy
  metric energy_consumption_twh f64
  metric energy_production_twh f64
  metric energy_consumption_per_capita_kwh f64
  metric energy_production_per_capita_kwh f64
  metric renewable_share f64
  metric electricity_usd_kwh f64
  metric co2_per_capita_t f64
  group career
  metric swe_median_usd f64
  metric tech_jobs u32
  metric mobility f64
  group fit
  # U+001F-joined ISO 639-1 codes spoken.
  col language str ?
  metric tech f64
  metric ease f64
  # U+001F-joined iso2 of citizenships that need no work permit here.
  col work_permit str ?
  # atlas_position and atlas_labeled: the atlas reads every place now (0003_atlas).
  retired col 2
  group prose
  prose liveability
  prose notes

# The atlas projection of places: every place is in the atlas now (0003_atlas).
retired table 1

table corporations world resident
  natural domain
  cap 50000
  index name
  group identity
  col domain str !
  col name str !
  col legal_name str ?
  col hq_place_id ref places ?
  col parent_id ref corporations ?
  col founded_year u32 ?
  col ownership enum ownership ?
  col ticker str ?
  col exchange str ?
  col industry str ?
  col sector str ?
  col linkedin_url str ?
  group size
  metric headcount u32
  metric engineers u32
  metric headcount_growth f64
  group private economics
  metric valuation_usd f64
  metric total_raised_usd f64
  col last_round str ?
  col last_round_on day ?
